msgstr "__PLUMED と Chemiscope で同様の図を作ってください。__ 色を変え、Beta-sheet 含有量も調べてください。"

# Literal notation or identifier intentionally preserved.
#: DIMENSIONALITY.md:184
msgid "MDS"
msgstr "MDS"

# 原文は非周期 CV に関する条件の記述が前後で矛盾している。翻訳では条件を独自に修正せず保持した。
#: DIMENSIONALITY.md:186
msgid ""
"In the previous section, we performed PCA on the atomic positions directly. "
"In the section before last, however, we also saw how we could store high-"
"dimensional vectors of collective variables and then use them as input to a "
"dimensionality reduction algorithm. Therefore, we might legitimately ask if "
"we can do PCA using these high-dimensional vectors as input rather than "
"atomic positions. The answer to this question is yes as long as the CV is "
"not periodic. If any of our CVs are not periodic, we cannot analyze them "
"using the PCA action. We can, however, formulate the PCA algorithm "
"differently. In this alternative formulation, which is known as classical "
"multidimensional scaling (MDS), we do the following:"
msgstr ""
"前節は原子位置の PCA でしたが、保存した高次元 CV Vector を入力にすることも、非周期 CV なら可能です。非周期 CV があると PCA "
"Action では解析できません。別の定式化、Classical Multidimensional Scaling (MDS) では次を行います。"

#: DIMENSIONALITY.md:191
msgid "We calculate the matrix of distances between configurations"
msgstr "Configuration 間距離の Matrix を求める。"

#: DIMENSIONALITY.md:192
msgid "We perform an operation known as centring the matrix."
msgstr "Matrix を Centering する。"

#: DIMENSIONALITY.md:193
msgid ""
"We diagonalize the centred matrix The eigenvectors multiplied by the "
"corresponding eigenvalue's square root can then be used as a set of "
"projections for our input points."
msgstr "Centering 後の Matrix を対角化し、Eigenvector に対応する Eigenvalue の平方根を掛けて射影とする。"

#: DIMENSIONALITY.md:196
msgid ""
"This method is used less often than PCA as the matrix that we have to "
"diagonalize here in the third step can be considerably larger than the "
"matrix that we have to diagonalize when we perform PCA. To avoid this "
"expensive diagonalization step, we often select a subset of so-called "
"landmark points on which to run the algorithm directly. Projections for the "
"remaining points are then found by using a so-called out-of-sample "
"procedure. This is what has been done in the following input:"
msgstr ""
"MDS は対角化する Matrix が PCA より大きくなり得るため、使用頻度が低めです。コストを避けるため Landmark "
"の部分集合に適用し、残りを Out-of-sample で射影します。次の入力が例です。"

#: DIMENSIONALITY.md:267
msgid ""
"This input collects all the torsional angles for the configurations in the "
"trajectory. Then, at the end of the calculation, the matrix of distances "
"between these points is computed, and a set of landmark points is selected "
"using a method known as farthest point sampling. A matrix that contains only"
" those distances between the landmarks is then constructed and diagonalized "
"by the CLASSICAL_MDS action so that projections of the landmarks can be "
"built. The final step is then to project the remainder of the trajectory "
"using the PROJECT_POINTS action. Try to fill in the blanks in the input "
"above and run this calculation now using the command:"
msgstr ""
"全 Torsion Angle を収集し、終了時に距離 Matrix を作り、Farthest Point Sampling で Landmark "
"を選びます。その距離 Matrix を CLASSICAL_MDS で対角化して Landmark を射影し、PROJECT_POINTS "
"で残りを射影します。空欄を埋め、次で実行してください。"

